 "notes": ["The input is one request. args.authorization is the value of its Authorization header: a text stands for the UTF-8 bytes of the text, a $base64 marker holds bytes that are not UTF-8, and null stands for a request with no such header.","context.token is the token that the service holds. A vector with params.token is for a service that holds that token in its place.","The generator gives the app the bytes of the header with no server between the two. A server removes each space and each tab at the two ends of a header value before the app gets the value.","context.token is the token of the one webhook that the route table holds. An accepted vector is a request that the listener starts a job for. A refused vector gets HTTP 404, the answer for a webhook that the listener does not know.","The web framework decodes the bytes of a header as Latin-1. The copy takes a text that starts with Bearer and one space, in that case of letters. It removes the whitespace of Python str.strip from the two ends of the rest. Then it encodes the rest as UTF-8 and compares the bytes with the token."],
